    "pressure": {
      "file": "digestion_autoclave_pressure.glb",
      "title": "High temperature and pressure dissolve the alumina",
      "description": "In digestion hot caustic liquor dissolves the alumina minerals: Al(OH)₃ + NaOH → NaAl(OH)₄. Gibbsitic bauxite digests at about 140–150 °C; boehmitic/diaspore bauxites need ~ 230–270 °C, which means pressures up to roughly 30–35 bar. Vessels in series give the residence time needed while keeping the slurry hot and well mixed.",
